      {
        "id": 151408,
        "name": "byc",
        "username": "byc",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/ebca7d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-14T22:11:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Just the obvious ones.</p>\n<p>I usually do Bunker and Wraith together in a fast game, not looking to win.  And then once I have it, I quit out.  Same with Tachyon, but she requires just a bit more time since it’s more cards involved.</p>\n<p>Haka and Scholar looks to be really good together, since it takes a bit of time to setup, and Savage Mana buys a lot of time (it’s not required, but it helps a lot burying targets under it).</p>\n<p>I usually do everything else by themselves since it’s easier to manage.</p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:30:15.362Z",
